※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4667
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4667 LANG_ITERATOR_LENDS
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4668 LANG_ITERATOR_MADE_HERE

※ An iterator reads what it walks when it walks it, so the names it reads are
※ lent to it while it is in scope, and writing one meanwhile is refused: every
※ walk then reads what the first would have.

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u6:
    let arr: mut u8⟦4⟧ = ⟦0u8, 1u8, 2u8, 3u8⟧
    let q := arr⟦arr > 1⟧
    arr⟦0⟧ ← 5u8
    let n: mut u8 = 0u8
    foreach x := q:
        n ← n + x
    if n = 5u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
